✅ Q12 — Find All Numbers That Appear Only Once

🎗️ 12.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<Integer> containing positive, negative, and zero values.
Using Java Streams, find all numbers that appear exactly once in the list.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as a List<Integer>.
🔴 Preserve the original encounter order.
🔴 Correctly handle positive and negative integers.
🔴 Correctly handle duplicate values.
🔴 Correctly handle zero.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Do not modify the original list.

🎗️ 12.2 Input / Output

👉 Input : List<Integer> numberList = List.of(10, 25, 10, -5, 40, 25, 15, -5, 30, 25);
👉 Expected Output : [40, 15, 30]

Because:

10 → appears 2 times ❌
25 → appears 3 times ❌
-5 → appears 2 times ❌
40 → appears 1 time ✅
15 → appears 1 time ✅
30 → appears 1 time ✅

🎗️ 12.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.
You can provide:

🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches you know
🔴 Your thoughts about empty-list behavior
🔴 How you preserve the original encounter order
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too